 ### Blinn-Phong Shading Model
-Uses the halfway vector $H = \frac{L+V}{|L+V|}$ instead of the reflection vector $R$ [S1]. It is computationally cheaper (no reflection vector calculation) and produces slightly different highlight shapes [G]. Choose when performance is critical or the specific highlight shape of Blinn-Phong is desired [2239-blinn-phong-shading-model.md].
