+*   **When not to use:** Physically based rendering (PBR) pipelines, scenes requiring accurate energy conservation, or when realistic shadowing and global illumination are needed [G].
 
 ## Background
-The Phong shading model was developed by Bui Tuong Phong in 1975 [S2, unofficial]. It was introduced as an empirical model to approximate the way light reflects off surfaces, specifically focusing on the specular highlight. It became a standard in computer graphics due to its simplicity and visual effectiveness. It is widely used in real-time rendering engines, educational contexts, and as a component in more complex lighting pipelines [S1][S2, unofficial]. The model is often implemented in fragment shaders in OpenGL pipelines [S2, unofficial].
